payload.message:
Findings from CLI probing of `/workspace/executable`:

**Help / Version**
- No args, `help`, and `--help` are identical: exit `0`, stdout only, header starts `direnv v2.37.1`.
- `-h` is not special. It is treated as a command lookup failure:
  - `./executable -h` -> exit `1`, stderr `\x1b[31mdirenv: error command "./executable -h" not found\x1b[0m`
  - the quoted command string reflects the original invocation text (`executable -h` if called from `PATH`).
- `version` and `--version` print bare `2.37.1\n` to stdout and exit `0`.
- `version 2.37.1`, `version v2.37.1`, `version 2.37.0` -> exit `0`, no output.
- `version 2.37.2` -> exit `1`, stderr `\x1b[31mdirenv: error current version v2.37.1 is older than the desired version v2.37.2\x1b[0m`
- `version foo` -> exit `1`, stderr `\x1b[31mdirenv: error vfoo is not a valid semver version\x1b[0m`

Normal `help` command list is:
- `allow [PATH_TO_RC]` with aliases `permit, grant`
- `block [PATH_TO_RC]` with aliases `deny, disallow, revoke`
- `edit [PATH_TO_RC]`
- `exec DIR COMMAND [...ARGS]`
- `export SHELL`
- `fetchurl <url> [<integrity-hash>]`
- `help [SHOW_PRIVATE]`
- `hook SHELL`
- `prune`
- `reload`
- `status [--json]`
- `stdlib`
- `version [VERSION_AT_LEAST]`
- `log [--status | --error] <message>`

Quirks:
- Canonical command is `block`, not `deny`; docs/man are stale here.
- `help` with any extra arg at all (`help true`, `help false`, `help 0`, `help foo`) shows private commands and appends `* = private commands`. Omitted arg hides them.
- In help, the `Supported SHELL values are: [...]` list order is nondeterministic across runs. I saw 10 unique orderings in 10 invocations.

Private commands shown when any help arg is present:
- `*apply_dump FILE`
- `*show_dump DUMP`
- `*check-required SHELL ENVRC_PATH PATH...`
- `*dotenv [SHELL] [PATH_TO_DOTENV]`
- `*dump [SHELL] [FILE]`
- `*watch SHELL PATH...`
- `*watch-dir SHELL DIR`
- `*watch-list [SHELL]`
- `*watch-print [--null]`
- `*current PATH`

**Hook**
Supported `hook` shells are exactly:
- `bash`
- `zsh`
- `fish`
- `tcsh`
- `elvish`
- `pwsh`
- `murex`

Errors:
- `hook` with no arg -> exit `1`, stderr `\x1b[31mdirenv: error unknown target shell ''\x1b[0m`
- `hook nu` -> exit `1`, stderr `\x1b[31mdirenv: error unknown target shell 'nu'\x1b[0m`

Important quirk:
- Hook output embeds the canonical real path `/workspace/executable`, even if invoked as `./executable`, through `PATH`, or via a symlink.
- `bash`, `zsh`, and `fish` outputs start with a leading blank line.
- `tcsh` and `murex` hook outputs have no trailing newline.

Exact hook outputs observed:

```sh
# hook bash

_direnv_hook() {
  local previous_exit_status=$?;
  vars="$("/workspace/executable" export bash)";
  trap -- '' SIGINT;
  eval "$vars";
  trap - SIGINT;
  return $previous_exit_status;
};
if [[ ";${PROMPT_COMMAND[*]:-};" != *";_direnv_hook;"* ]]; then
  if [[ "$(declare -p PROMPT_COMMAND 2>&1)" == "declare -a"* ]]; then
    PROMPT_COMMAND=(_direnv_hook "${PROMPT_COMMAND[@]}")
  else
    PROMPT_COMMAND="_direnv_hook${PROMPT_COMMAND:+;$PROMPT_COMMAND}"
  fi
fi
```

```sh
# hook zsh

_direnv_hook() {
  vars="$("/workspace/executable" export zsh)"
  trap -- '' SIGINT
  eval "$vars"
  trap - SIGINT
}
typeset -ag precmd_functions
if (( ! ${precmd_functions[(I)_direnv_hook]} )); then
  precmd_functions=(_direnv_hook $precmd_functions)
fi
typeset -ag chpwd_functions
if (( ! ${chpwd_functions[(I)_direnv_hook]} )); then
  chpwd_functions=(_direnv_hook $chpwd_functions)
fi
```

```fish
# hook fish

    function __direnv_export_eval --on-event fish_prompt;
        "/workspace/executable" export fish | source;

        if test "$direnv_fish_mode" != "disable_arrow";
            function __direnv_cd_hook --on-variable PWD;
                if test "$direnv_fish_mode" = "eval_after_arrow";
                    set -g __direnv_export_again 0;
                else;
                    "/workspace/executable" export fish | source;
                end;
            end;
        end;
    end;

    function __direnv_export_eval_2 --on-event fish_preexec;
        if set -q __direnv_export_again;
            set -e __direnv_export_again;
            "/workspace/executable" export fish | source;
            echo;
        end;

        functions --erase __direnv_cd_hook;
    end;
```

```tcsh
# hook tcsh
alias precmd 'eval `/workspace/executable export tcsh`'
```

```elvish
# hook elvish
## hook for direnv
set @edit:before-readline = $@edit:before-readline {
	try {
		var m = [("/workspace/executable" export elvish | from-json)]
		if (> (count $m) 0) {
			set m = (all $m)
			keys $m | each { |k|
				if $m[$k] {
					set-env $k $m[$k]
				} else {
					unset-env $k
				}
			}
		}
	} catch e {
		echo $e
	}
}
```

```powershell
# hook pwsh
using namespace System;
using namespace System.Management.Automation;

if ($PSVersionTable.PSVersion.Major -lt 7 -or ($PSVersionTable.PSVersion.Major -eq 7 -and $PSVersionTable.PSVersion.Minor -lt 2)) {
    throw "direnv: PowerShell version $($PSVersionTable.PSVersion) does not meet the minimum required version 7.2!"
}

$hook = [EventHandler[LocationChangedEventArgs]] {
  param([object] $source, [LocationChangedEventArgs] $eventArgs)
  end {
    $export = (/workspace/executable export pwsh) -join [Environment]::NewLine;
    if ($export) {
      Invoke-Expression -Command $export;
    }
  }
};
$currentAction = $ExecutionContext.SessionState.InvokeCommand.LocationChangedAction;
if ($currentAction) {
  $ExecutionContext.SessionState.InvokeCommand.LocationChangedAction = [Delegate]::Combine($currentAction, $hook);
}
else {
  $ExecutionContext.SessionState.InvokeCommand.LocationChangedAction = $hook;
};
```

```murex
# hook murex
event: onPrompt direnv_hook=before {
	"/workspace/executable" export murex -> set exports
	if { $exports != "" } {
		$exports -> :json: formap key value {
			if { is-null value } then {
				!export "$key"
			} else {
				$value -> export "$key"
			}
		}
	}
}
```

**Export**
Supported `export` formats are exactly:
- `bash`
- `zsh`
- `fish`
- `tcsh`
- `elvish`
- `pwsh`
- `murex`
- `json`
- `vim`
- `gha`
- `gzenv`
- `systemd`

Errors:
- `export` with no arg -> exit `1`, stderr `\x1b[31mdirenv: error unknown target shell ''\x1b[0m`
- `export nu` -> exit `1`, stderr `\x1b[31mdirenv: error unknown target shell 'nu'\x1b[0m`

Behavior in isolated temp dir with no `.envrc`:
- `export bash` and `export json` both exit `0` with completely empty stdout/stderr.

Behavior with blocked `.envrc` (`export FOO=bar`), fresh HOME/XDG:
- `export bash` / `export json` still emit metadata (`DIRENV_DIFF`, `DIRENV_WATCHES`, `DIRENV_DIR`, `DIRENV_FILE`) on stdout, but do not include `FOO`.
- exit is `1`.
- stderr is red error: `direnv: error /tmp/.../.envrc is blocked. Run \`direnv allow\` to approve its content`

Behavior with allowed `.envrc` containing:
```sh
unset OLD
export FOO="bar baz"
```
and initial env `OLD=gone`:
- stderr on every successful export is two reset-colored lines:
  - `\x1b[0mdirenv: loading /tmp/.../.envrc`
  - `\x1b[0mdirenv: export +FOO -OLD`
- stdout always includes internal vars `DIRENV_DIFF`, `DIRENV_DIR`, `DIRENV_FILE`, `DIRENV_WATCHES` plus the actual env changes.

Format notes from that sample:
- `bash`: semicolon-separated `unset`/`export`, `$'...'` quoting, no trailing newline. Statement order is nondeterministic across runs.
- `zsh`: same general style as bash, also no trailing newline.
- `fish`: `set -x -g` / `set -e -g`, semicolon-separated, no trailing newline.
- `tcsh`: one-line `setenv` / `unsetenv` script, no trailing newline, spaces escaped as `\ `. I repeatedly saw odd mangling of values ending in `==`, e.g. `...TAAD__0eGkh4"=" ;`.
- `elvish`: single-line JSON object with `null` for removals, trailing newline.
- `pwsh`: one line like `Remove-Item -LiteralPath 'env:/OLD';${env:FOO}='bar baz';...`, no trailing newline.
- `murex`: same JSON object shape as `elvish`, trailing newline.
- `json`: pretty-printed JSON object with `null` for removals, no trailing newline.
- `vim`: `call setenv('KEY','VALUE')` per line, `v:null` for removals, trailing newline.
- `gha`: `NAME<<ghadelimiter_<32 hex>` heredoc blocks, trailing newline. Removed vars are omitted entirely.
- `systemd`: `KEY=value` lines, trailing newline. Removed vars are omitted entirely.
- `gzenv`: one long line, no trailing newline. Decoding it shows it is URL-safe unpadded base64 of zlib-compressed JSON equivalent to `json`.

Extra export quirk:
- At least `bash`, `zsh`, and `tcsh` export statement ordering is nondeterministic across invocations.

